    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1192-a1">

                <pb facs="1393" n="1195" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1195"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure A]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Draft</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the Combined
                        Shipping Adjustment Board</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The Combined Chiefs of Staff have been studying the problem of providing
                        passenger carrying shipping to meet the urgent demands for the essential
                        military operations in the prosecution of the war against Japan, and for the
                        provision of such shipping of this type to <pb facs="1394" n="1196"
                            xml:id="pg1196"/> meet other requirements as can be made available
                        without adversely affecting military operations.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The available passenger space is insufficient to meet all the urgent
                        requirements of the United Nations, and coordination of demands is,
                        therefore, essential in order to determine priority and to secure shipping
                        efficiency as well as to ensure the fullest consideration being given to all
                        claimants.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The Combined Chiefs of Staff have, therefore, agreed that in accordance
                        with the “Agreement on Principles,” dated 5 August 1944, contained in the
                        UMA report, October, 1944, the following procedure in respect of the
                        submission of demands should be adopted by all the Allied nations:—<anchor
                            n="3" xml:id="d1192-f1"/></item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <list>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Vital demands for shipping should therefore be submitted to the United
                        Maritime Authority for consideration.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>The Combined Shipping Adjustment Board is requested to transmit the
                        foregoing statement of policy to the United Maritime Executive Board in
                        Washington and London.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1192-f1" n="3" xml:id="d1192-f1-content">
                <p>Here follow subparagraphs <hi rendition="#italic">a, b</hi>, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>, which are identical with paragraphs 4 <hi
                        rendition="#italic">a, b</hi>, and <hi rendition="#italic">c</hi> in the
                    body of the Committee’s report printed above, except that the parenthetical
                    “(UMA)” in subparagraph <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi> is omitted.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
